# Terrain and placement share one grid, so the board is what it looks like.
#   .  open        #  wall        O  pit        ^  spikes      H  high ground
#   A  Player A deploy slot       B  Player B deploy slot
#   any other letter = an enemy declared by a 'spawn' line below

id: hz-08-free-kick
number: 208
name: Free Kick
pool: Ordinary
description: Four pits with room to stand around them. Dropping something in only half kills it — finishing it from the rim is free, and so is what they do to you.
retired: superseded by hz-08-free-kick-v2, which carries the same thesis over connected blocking mass and a question still live on round 3 (D-280). Kept parseable: the replay logs of every run that played it still name this id.
design: Hazard Pressure 8 of 10 — clinging is not dying.
design: A unit shoved into a pit clings, holds its activation slot, and is only Voided at the end of the following round — unless somebody adjacent finishes it, which costs neither half of an activation. Each of the four pits has open tiles on several sides, so the second unit you bring is not wasted: it stands by the rim and takes the free kick.
design: The HighGround at (1,4) is the trap: fall damage lands while the unit is already clinging, and any damage to a clinging unit Voids it outright. Being shoved off there into the pit below is not a rescue problem, it is instant.

spawn h = Husk
spawn g = Grappler
spawn s = Stalker

roster a: Vanguard, Archer
roster b: Threadcaster, Wardbearer

board:
  ..h.h.B
  .O...OB
  ^.....B
  .......
  .H...g^
  AO...O.
  AA.s.h#
